Create SG Quiet Design System starter.

Goal:
Reusable minimal design foundation.

Style:
- minimal, calm
- neutral colors
- strong spacing
- subtle borders
- minimal accent
- no visual noise, heavy gradients, or clutter

Structure:

SwiftUI:
DesignSystem/
- SGColors.swift
- SGSpacing.swift
- SGTypography.swift
- SGRadius.swift
- SGShadows.swift
- SGButton.swift
- SGCard.swift
- SGInput.swift
- SGToolbarStyle.swift

Web:
src/design-system/
- tokens.ts
- components/
  - SGButton.tsx
  - SGCard.tsx
  - SGInput.tsx
  - SGToolbar.tsx

Rules:
- If SwiftUI → implement SwiftUI
- If web → implement web
- If both → ask first

Tokens:

Colors:
paperLight #F8F5EE
paperDark #232220
surfaceLight #FFFFFF
surfaceDark #2C2C2C
textLight #1C1C1C
textDark #F5F5F5
textSecondary #8A8A8A
accent #9D42F0
accentSubtle #CFA8FF
borderLight #E5E5E5
borderDark #3A3A3A

Spacing:
4, 8, 16, 24, 32, 48

Radius:
6, 10, 16, 999

Typography:
body 16
small 12
sectionTitle 18 semibold
mainTitle 28 semibold
SF Pro (Apple), Inter/system (web)

Components:

SGButton:
- ~44 height
- subtle border
- medium radius
- primary = accent
- secondary = neutral
- disabled = opacity

SGCard:
- subtle border
- soft bg
- padding md/lg
- radius lg

SGInput:
- calm border
- accent focus
- readable

SGToolbar:
- minimal, compact
- horizontal
- non-dominant

Constraints:
- do not break logic
- no unrelated refactor
- use tokens only

Output:
- create files
- show added files
- give 1 usage example
